The Multi-Step Quiz App with a Timer is the perfect finale because it combines state management (tracking scores and current questions), timing functions, and conditional rendering (swapping screens without a page refresh).
## 1. The Structure (index.html)
We’ll create a wrapper that holds three main states: the "Start" screen, the "Quiz" area, and the "Results" screen.

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>JS Master Quiz</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div class="quiz-container" id="quiz">
        <div id="start-screen">
            <h1>Ready for the Quiz?</h1>
            <button id="start-btn">Start Quiz</button>
        </div>

        <div id="quiz-screen" class="hide">
            <div class="header">
                <div id="timer">Time left: <span>15</span>s</div>
                <div id="score">Score: 0</div>
            </div>
            <h2 id="question">Question text goes here?</h2>
            <div id="answer-buttons" class="btn-grid">
                <!-- Buttons injected by JS -->
            </div>
            <button id="next-btn" class="hide">Next Question</button>
        </div>

        <div id="result-screen" class="hide">
            <h1>Quiz Finished!</h1>
            <p>Your final score is: <span id="final-score">0</span></p>
            <button onclick="location.reload()">Restart</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>

